#  Autism Prediction System

This project is a machine learning-based web application developed using **Streamlit**, **pandas**, **numpy**, and **scikit-learn** to predict the likelihood of **Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)** in adults. It uses user inputs from a standard screening test and outputs a prediction in real-time.

---

##  Features

- Predicts likelihood of ASD using questionnaire inputs.
- Easy-to-use web interface built with Streamlit.
- Uses a trained Random Forest model.
- Lightweight and fast — runs locally.

---

## Technologies Used

- **Python 3.x**
- **pandas** – for data manipulation
- **numpy** – for numerical operations
- **scikit-learn** – for machine learning
- **Streamlit** – for building the web app
- **pickle** – to save/load the trained model

---

## 📁 Dataset

The dataset used is the **Autism Screening Adult Data Set**, available from:
- UCI Machine Learning Repository
- [Kaggle: Autism Screening Adult Data](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/felipefzm/autism-screening-adults)


